course: dictionary
lesson: 13942
title: A letdown
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: A letdown is a disappointment. It is something that was not as good as you hoped it would be. «The film was a letdown.» You expected it to be exciting, but it was dull, so you feel let down. A letdown is a noun, so you can say «a letdown» or «letdowns».
explain: The words around a word give clues. «We waited all day for the match, but the rain stopped it. What a letdown!» Waiting all day and then having no match tells you that letdown means a sad, disappointing moment. The exclamation shows the feeling.
explain: Let down can also be a verb phrase. «Dad promised to take us to the zoo, but he let us down.» Here, to let someone down means to disappoint them by not doing what you promised. The word down is part of the phrase, so the meaning is not about lowering anything.
fact: A letdown is a disappointment, something not as good as you hoped.
fact: «Letdown» is an informal word, so you will hear it in everyday talk and stories.
fact: To let someone down means to disappoint them by not doing what you promised.
fact: «What a letdown!» is a common phrase when something turns out worse than expected.
fact: Check the meaning by swapping in «disappointment»: «The film was a disappointment» still makes sense.
exercise: «The sequel was a letdown after the brilliant first film.» What is a letdown? | A loud, happy cheer | A very big, heavy book | *A disappointment, something not as good as hoped
exercise: «Dad promised to take us to the zoo, but he let us down.» What does let us down mean here? | He took us to the zoo after all | *He disappointed us by not doing what he promised | He lowered us to the ground
exercise: «The match was cancelled. What a letdown!» Which word tells you how the speaker feels? | *letdown | the | cancelled | match
test: «We planned a picnic, but the weather was awful. It was a letdown.» What does letdown mean? | *A disappointment | A long journey | A new game | A surprise treat
test: «My friend said she would help me, but she didn't turn up. She let me down.» What does let me down mean? | She gave me a present | She lent me her bike | She put me on the floor | *She disappointed me by not doing what she promised
exam: «The new café was a letdown; the cake was dry and the service was slow.» What does a letdown mean here? | *Something that disappointed the hopes we had | A happy surprise | A kind of cake | A large, busy place
